#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-"
"primitives}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Input: Abstract circuit.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Output: Quasi-probability distribution.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Use the `StatevectorSampler` primitive from Qiskit to reconstruct a quasi-"
"probability distribution of states yielded from sampling the circuit. For "
"the task of generating a kernel matrix, we are particularly interested in "
"the probability of measuring the |0> state.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/quantum-kernel-"
"training/extracted-outputs/step3-small-code-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 4: Post-process and return result in desired classical format "
